g before Osvaldo in the attic in area C24.","textAlpha":1,"textColor":"#FFFFFF","texture":null,"x":212.5,"y":537.5,"z":0},{"_id":"OMqXWiPaUojII3Tk","author":"ZWZhNTMzZTE2NzI3","bezierFactor":0,"fillAlpha":0.1,"fillColor":"#FFFFFF","fillType":0,"flags":{"perfect-vision":{"enabled":false,"fit":false,"prototype":null},"tagger":{}},"fontFamily":"Signika","fontSize":48,"hidden":false,"locked":false,"rotation":0,"shape":{"height":263,"points":[],"radius":null,"type":"r","width":1275},"strokeAlpha":1,"strokeColor":"#FFFFFF","strokeWidth":8,"text":"Lord Victoro Cassalanter: Roll 1d100. 01-70 He's in his office (area C6). 71-90 He's in the reading room (area C4). 91-100 he's with Ammalia at one of her three locations.","textAlpha":1,"textColor":"#FFFFFF","texture":null,"x":225,"y":962.5,"z":0},{"_id":"cfs1nP1k7I4R9wE4","author":"ZWZhNTMzZTE2NzI3","bezierFactor":0,"fillAlpha":0.1,"fillColor":"#FFFFFF","fillType":0,"flags":{"perfect-vision":{"enabled":false,"fit":false,"prototype":null},"tagger":{}},"fontFamily":"Signika","fontSize":48,"hidden":false,"locked":false,"rotation":0,"shape":{"height":263,"points":[],"radius":null,"type":"r","width":1275},"strokeAlpha":1,"strokeColor":"#FFFFFF","strokeWidth":8,"text":"Terenzio and Elzerina Cassalanter: Roll 1d100. 01-50, they're playing in their room (area C18). 51-75 They're in the library (C3). 76-100 They're chasing butterflies in the garden (area C25).","textAlpha":1,"textColor":"#FFFFFF","texture":null,"x":225,"y":1362.5,"z":0},{"_id":"aSm1OcHsm6QwlEtE","author":"ZWZhNTMzZTE2NzI3","bezierFactor":0,"fillAlpha":0.1,"fillColor":"#FFFFFF","fillType":0,"flags":{"perfect-vision":{"enabled":false,"fit":false,"prototype":null},"tagger":{}},"fontFamily":"Signika","fontSize":48,"hidden":false,"locked":false,"rotation":0,"shape":{"height":225,"points":[],"radius":null,"type":"r","width":1275},"strokeAlpha":1,"strokeColor":"#FFFFFF","strokeWidth":8,"text":"The below three head servants are noted as cult fanatics but are in disguise as tiefling servants. Replace their tokens with the image of a tiefling.","textAlpha":1,"textColor":"#FFFFFF","texture":null,"x":213,"y":2338,"z":0},{"_id":"JtsphZinquf94FPe","author":"ZWZhNTMzZTE2NzI3","bezierFactor":0,"fillAlpha":0.1,"fillColor":"#FFFFFF","fillType":0,"flags":{"perfect-vision":{"enabled":false,"fit":false,"prototype":null},"tagger":{}},"fontFamily":"Signika","fontSize":48,"hidden":false,"locked":false,"rotation":0,"shape":{"height":175,"points":[],"radius":null,"type":"r","width":1287},"strokeAlpha":1,"strokeColor":"#FFFFFF","strokeWidth":8,"text":"On founders day several nobles and 100 of Waterdeep's poorest comoners gather on the lawn, ballroom, the entry, dining room and foyer","textAlpha":1,"textColor":"#FFFFFF","texture":null,"x":188,"y":6613,"z":0},{"_id":"W68WrbQa6ASXymIL","author":"ZWZhNTMzZTE2NzI3","bezierFactor":0,"fillAlpha":0.1,"fillColor":"#FFFFFF","fillType":0,"flags":{"perfect-vision":{"enabled":false,"fit":false,"prototype":null},"tagger":{}},"fontFamily":"Signika","fontSize":48,"hidden":false,"locked":false,"rotation":0,"shape":{"height":413,"points":[],"radius":null,"type":"r","width":1302},"strokeAlpha":1,"strokeColor":"#FFFFFF","strokeWidth":8,"text":"Four doppelgangers from the Yawning Portal have slipped into the party disguised as nobles. Their leader, Bonnie (see “Familiar Faces” journal entry), poses as a minor noblewoman going by the name Lymeria Lhaurilstar; she was hoping to have a fun night at the party, but she’s willing to help the characters if they need aid.  NOTE: REMEMBER TO CHANGE THE TOKEN PICTURE TO A NOBLE.","textAlpha":1,"textColor":"#FFFFFF","texture":null,"x":188,"y":6925,"z":0}],"flags":{"ddb":{"bookCode":"wdh","cobaltId":null,"contentChunkId":"ddb-missing-wdh-103090","ddbId":103090,"foundryVersion":"10.291","noteInfos":[{"cobaltId":null,"contentChunkIdStart":"003b7f15-fc01-42cc-a344-0c9a0b370e40","contentChunkIdStop":"EOF","ddbId":62,"parentId":561,"sceneName":"Cassalanter Villa","slug":"hell-of-a-summer#Cassal